From: Jonas <developer@raccoon.ing>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] u-boot: sun60iw2: add PCIe host controller and NVMe boot support for Allwinner A733

Enable PCIe root complex (CONFIG_PCIE_ALLWINNER_RC, CONFIG_AW_CADENCE_COMBOPHY),
PCI bus layer (CONFIG_DM_PCI), block layer (CONFIG_AW_BLK), and NVMe driver
(CONFIG_NVME, CONFIG_CMD_NVME, CONFIG_CMD_PCI) in sun60iw2p1_a733_defconfig.

Fix uninitialized compiler warnings in drivers/pci/pci-uclass.c preventing
Werror builds, and enable automated distro boot command scanning for NVMe:
"pci enum; nvme scan; setenv devnum 0; run nvme_boot;"

Signed-off-by: Jonas <developer@raccoon.ing>
---
diff --git a/configs/sun60iw2p1_a733_defconfig b/configs/sun60iw2p1_a733_defconfig
index 6581b6b7..fff4d51c 100644
--- a/configs/sun60iw2p1_a733_defconfig
+++ b/configs/sun60iw2p1_a733_defconfig
@@ -95,3 +95,14 @@ CONFIG_CMD_EXT4_WRITE=y
 CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_EXT4=y
 #CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_SUNXI_FLASH=y
 
+CONFIG_AW_BLK=y
+CONFIG_CMD_PCI=y
+CONFIG_CMD_NVME=y
+CONFIG_PCI=y
+CONFIG_DM_PCI=y
+CONFIG_PCIE_ALLWINNER_RC=y
+CONFIG_AW_CADENCE_COMBOPHY=y
+CONFIG_NVME=y
+CONFIG_PCIE_POWER_GPIO="PL3"
+CONFIG_PCIE_PERST_GPIO="PD22"
+CONFIG_PCIE_WAKE_GPIO="PD21"
diff --git a/drivers/pci/pci-uclass.c b/drivers/pci/pci-uclass.c
index 46e9c71b..3fb97fcc 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pci-uclass.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci-uclass.c
@@ -474,7 +474,7 @@ int dm_pci_clrset_config32(struct udevice *dev, int offset, u32 clr, u32 set)
 static void set_vga_bridge_bits(struct udevice *dev)
 {
 	struct udevice *parent = dev->parent;
-	u16 bc;
+	u16 bc = 0;
 
 	while (parent->seq != 0) {
 		dm_pci_read_config16(parent, PCI_BRIDGE_CONTROL, &bc);
@@ -1155,7 +1155,7 @@ int pci_get_regions(struct udevice *dev, struct pci_region **iop,
 
 u32 dm_pci_read_bar32(struct udevice *dev, int barnum)
 {
-	u32 addr;
+	u32 addr = 0;
 	int bar;
 
 	bar = PCI_BASE_ADDRESS_0 + barnum * 4;
@@ -1304,7 +1304,7 @@ pci_addr_t dm_pci_phys_to_bus(struct udevice *dev, phys_addr_t phys_addr,
 void *dm_pci_map_bar(struct udevice *dev, int bar, int flags)
 {
 	pci_addr_t pci_bus_addr;
-	u32 bar_response;
+	u32 bar_response = 0;
 
 	/* read BAR address */
 	dm_pci_read_config32(dev, bar, &bar_response);
